Darknight remarks:
:        What the hell good are bags, anyway.  (ie. the normal ones?)
:Do they actually allow you to carry more?
:        It seems to me you should be allowed to wear them over your
:head to cover your face...  This would make you blind, and for those
:really ugly players, prevent you from aggravating monsters...  You
:could even cut eye holes in the bag and impersonate the Elephant Man.
     Well, they allow you to carry more different objects (it's hard
for someone without gauntlets of power to carry 52 different objects
at once anyway, but if you do have the gauntlets, it can be helpful to
store a lot of the less-often used items in a bag).  Since Nethack
assigns a letter to every object in your inventory, you can't carry
more than 52.
     The main problem with the bag is that it's a real pain to transfer
items in and out of them; you have to go through your whole inventory
(or the whole list of what's in the bag) until you find what you want.
     I think a better way of handling things would be to use a ctrl-I
command ("What container do you want an iventory of? [a-dz or *?] ")
to list, using a set of letters, the items in the sack, JUST LIKE it
does in your inventory.  When you (a)pply the sack, it should ask you
whether you want to put things in or take things out, and then prompt
you with a "Put what objects in? [a-ghzB-M or ?*]" or a "Take what
objects out? [a-cg or ?*]" and you could type as many object letters as
you please and then a <return> to do the whole sequence, e.g.
"You remove: N - a +5 wide sword named Stormbringer --MORE--
O - 15 potions of holy water --MORE--
Your pack cannot carry any more items"
(If it were a bag of holding, you might also get "You cannot carry
enough to remove a blessed +6 gauntlets of power").
     Similarly, since one can pick up (I'd also advise revising the
picking up sequence in a similar way) or drop many objects in one turn
as-is using the D command (if that's a bug, one could always use one
turn for each transfer and give a "You stop [dropping/picking
up/retrieving/stashing] objects --MORE-- Demogorgon hits! --MORE--"
etc.) why not allow players to list more than one object using the d
command, so it'd be "Drop which objects? [q-sA-Z or ?*]" and the player
could type in any number of letters and a <return>.
     Anyway, that's my two pence.

     A question: It seems that no matter what I do with a character, he
ends up aggravating monsters at some point.  This happens if I kill my
pet (I never eat it) after dumping him on level 1, or if I keep him, or
if I dump him on level 1 and don't ever come back.
     Is it a scroll I read somewhere?  Seems that permanent aggravation
of monsters is a bit heavy for a simple scroll.

"Hello Shadow, welcome to Nethack! --MORE--
